                <pb facs="0271" n="201" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg201"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119 P 43/924: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Special Representative</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">House</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-26T17:00:00-05:00"
                            >November 26, 1918—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. Your 123 November 19, 7 p.m. Suggestion that Gibson remain in Austria with headquarters in Vienna approved.
                    Not thought advisable to open Embassy Chancery. It is presumed Hoover will open headquarters’ office in Vienna
                    and Gibson should be able to use that
                    office in the capacity of assistant to Hoover.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
